From 9691ff91e074ed88c2a55b1028d909c925514cf3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aadharsh Pannirselvam <aadharsh@archetype.fund>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 23:03:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] gdf: a NEON gdf_inference_unit

Eight pixels per step. Per-class constants come from one byte-table lookup
per input (vqtbl1q_u8) instead of the AVX2 gather-and-swap; inputs stay in
int16 and only the three accumulators widen to int32. The vertical and
horizontal sparsity masks swap meaning with class parity (the AVX2 code
swaps sums 0 and 1 for odd classes), so they can only skip both sums
together. Columns past the last multiple of 8 go to the C kernel.

Bit-exact: 600 randomized unit trials against gdf_inference_unit_c (intra
and all inter tables, every qp table, both bit-depth shifts, odd tails),
and 18 of 18 whole decodes against pristine AVM. Single-threaded decode of
a 1600x2400 10-bit 4:4:4 still on an M3 Max: 314 ms to 127 ms.
---
